<Project>

  <!-- Solution-wide build governance. Applies to every project under the repo root
       (src/PtcXaeMcp.* — the WinForms host and the four test projects).

       Goal: surface the latent defect classes the codebase audit flagged (CS86xx
       nullable, CAxxxx correctness/reliability analyzers) instead of letting them
       compile silently. Phase 1 = inventory: analyzers ON, warnings NOT yet fatal.
       Once the warning inventory is triaged, flip TreatWarningsAsErrors per family
       (see the staged-rollout block at the bottom). -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- Single source of truth for the release version (issue #157 item 3). The SDK
         propagates this into AssemblyVersion/FileVersion/InformationalVersion for every
         project under the repo root, so McpBridge's ServerInfo.Version and the /health
         endpoint (both read via McpBridge.ThisAssemblyVersion(), which reads the
         InformationalVersion attribute) and the setup installer (setup/setup.iss, given
         explicitly via `/DAppVersion=1.3.0` — see setup/setup.iss for the publish command)
         all report the same number. Bump this single value on release; nothing else needs
         to change. -->
    <Version>2.2.0</Version>

    <!-- Display name in the exe's file properties; technical names (exe, folders) stay ptc-xae-mcp. -->
    <Product>Pneutronic XAE MCP</Product>
    <Company>Pneutronic AG</Company>

    <!-- Centralized so the per-project copies (already in all 5 csproj) inherit one source. -->
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>

    <!-- .NET analyzers are on by default for net5+, but make it explicit and lift the
         analysis level so reliability/correctness rules (CA2xxx) actually report. -->
    <EnableNETAnalyzers>true</EnableNETAnalyzers>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
    <AnalysisMode>Recommended</AnalysisMode>

    <!-- Surface the full picture during inventory: report all warnings, don't cap. -->
    <WarningLevel>9999</WarningLevel>

    <!-- Phase 1: keep the build green so we get a COMPLETE warning list rather than a
         hard stop. Do NOT set TreatWarningsAsErrors=true here yet. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================================================================
       STAGED ROLLOUT (enable after the inventory is triaged):

       Step 1: promote the highest-value nullable family to errors first.
         PropertyGroup with:
           WarningsAsErrors = CS8600;CS8602;CS8603;CS8604;CS8625;CS8629

       Step 2: once those are clean, flip everything and exempt the rest until fixed.
         PropertyGroup with:
           TreatWarningsAsErrors = true
           WarningsNotAsErrors   = (families still being worked, e.g. CA1822;CA1310)
       ============================================================================ -->

  <!-- CA1304/CA1305/CA1310 are fixed to zero in every project of the solution (issue #157
       item 6 — see CONTRIBUTING.md for the culture rule these fixes follow; the test
       projects followed in the last #157 pass) and promoted to build errors everywhere. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CA1304;CA1305;CA1310</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- ============================================================================
       ANALYZER WARNING BUDGET (issue #157 item 6) — PtcXaeMcp.WinForms only (the
       production project; test-project counts, e.g. CA1707 on underscore-named
       [Fact]s, are expected and out of scope here), from `dotnet test
       src/PtcXaeMcp.Tests` build output on 2026-09-27 (chore/release-polish-4 —
       CA1305 (193→0) and CA1310 (3→0) are now fixed and promoted to
       WarningsAsErrors above; every other count is unchanged from
       chore/release-polish-3):

          16  CA2249  string.IndexOf/StartsWith could use string.Contains
          14  CA1859  use the concrete type instead of the interface for a
                       COM/interop-typed field/variable (perf)
          13  CA1507  use nameof() instead of a string literal
           8  CA1838  avoid StringBuilder in P/Invoke signatures
           8  CA1822  member does not access instance data, could be static
           7  CA1869  reuse a cached JsonSerializerOptions instance
           4  CA1862  case-insensitive string comparison via ToLower/ToUpper
           3  CA2263  use the generic GetService<T>()/Enum.Parse<T>() overload
           3  CA1865  use a char overload instead of a single-char string
           3  CA1861  hoist a repeated constant array literal
           2  CA1068  CancellationToken parameter should be the last parameter
           1  CA2201  reserved exception type (OutOfMemoryException et al.) thrown
                       directly
           1  CA1870  hoist a repeated SearchValues<char> literal
           1  CA1846  use span-based StringBuilder.Append overload
           1  CA1845  use string.Concat(span) instead of "a" + b + "c"
           1  CA1510  ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(...) instead of a manual null-check throw

       Already fixed in earlier passes (no longer in the count above): CA1304 (the last
       site, ComMemberProbe.InvokeNoArgs, passes InvariantCulture; promoted with CA1305/CA1310),
       CA1001 (McpBridge
       now implements IDisposable), CA2101 (Win32DialogAutomation.SendMessage's string
       overload now marshals CharSet.Unicode), all 10 CA1806 sites (ignored P/Invoke/
       TryParse return values, now explicit discards), CS0618 (TwinCatComSession.
       AdsVariable.cs now calls RpcMethodExtension.IsVoid(method) instead of the obsolete
       IRpcMethod.IsVoid property), and the culture-dependent DateTime.TryParse in
       LicenseInfoParser.ParseDate (B-19, now InvariantCulture).

       Do NOT flip TreatWarningsAsErrors while this list is non-empty — see the staged
       rollout above. CA1304/CA1305/CA1310 are the only families promoted so far; every
       other rule above remains a warning until its own dedicated pass.
       ============================================================================ -->

</Project>
